ath12k: ahb: let remoteproc own the user PD when it already does

On IPQ5332 the multipd remoteproc driver can be told to register an rproc
per user PD, which is how the vendor device tree describes this hardware:
its wifi node points qcom,rproc at the user PD itself. This driver instead
treats qcom,rproc as the root PD and then loads, PAS authenticates and
spawns the user PD on its own.

Both cannot be true at once. With the vendor DT shape the PD boots and this
driver then cannot have the interrupt it needs:

  remoteproc remoteproc2: remote processor pd1 is now up
  genirq: Flags mismatch irq 31. 00002001 (UserPD1-spawn)
          vs. 00002001 (q6v5_wcss_userpd1_spawn-ack)
  ath12k_ahb c000000.wifi: error -EBUSY: Request spawn irq failed: -16

Doing the load here instead does not work with vendor firmware either. The
images are linked for a single loader filling one region -- q6_fw0 up to
0x4ab51000, q6_fw3 at 0x4aefd000, q6_fw1 at 0x4b2a3000 -- so q6_fw1 falls
below the per-PD window at 0x4bd00000 and the load fails as "segment
outside memory range", while widening the window to the whole Q6 region
lets it succeed and then kills the running root PD.

Detect the case from the device tree rather than adding a new property: a
user PD node is the one carrying a "spawn" smem state. When qcom,rproc
resolves to such a node, skip the interrupt request and let remoteproc
drive the PD.

Keep the boot itself in power_up(). ath12k_ahb_configure_rproc() runs
during probe, and booting there starts the QMI handshake before the rest
of the driver is ready for it; the firmware then reports a fatal error a
few hundred milliseconds later. Deferring to power_up() restores the
ordering this driver already relies on everywhere else.

This is a local patch. Upstream still has to decide which of the two models
is intended; see the discussion on linux-remoteproc.

Signed-off-by: Hideo Sumi <hideo.sumi@mugops.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
@@ -338,6 +338,35 @@
 	ath12k_ce_cleanup_pipes(ab);
 }
 
+/* Defined below; power_up() needs it before its definition. */
+static int ath12k_ahb_boot_root_pd(struct ath12k_base *ab);
+
+/*
+ * The multipd remoteproc driver creates a device per user PD, and a user PD
+ * node is the one carrying the "spawn" smem state. When qcom,rproc resolves
+ * to such a node, remoteproc owns the image, the PAS authentication and the
+ * spawn handshake, so this driver must not do any of it: both of them
+ * requesting the same spawn interrupt fails the second requester with
+ * -EBUSY, and the vendor firmware is in any case linked for a single loader
+ * filling one region, which this driver cannot reproduce from its own per-PD
+ * memory window.
+ */
+static bool ath12k_ahb_rproc_owns_userpd(struct ath12k_base *ab)
+{
+	struct ath12k_ahb *ab_ahb = ath12k_ab_to_ahb(ab);
+	struct device *rproc_dev;
+
+	if (!ab_ahb->tgt_rproc)
+		return false;
+
+	rproc_dev = ab_ahb->tgt_rproc->dev.parent;
+	if (!rproc_dev || !rproc_dev->of_node)
+		return false;
+
+	return of_property_match_string(rproc_dev->of_node,
+					"qcom,smem-state-names", "spawn") >= 0;
+}
+
 static int ath12k_ahb_power_up(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
 	struct ath12k_ahb *ab_ahb = ath12k_ab_to_ahb(ab);
@@ -353,6 +382,9 @@
 	u32 pasid;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (ath12k_ahb_rproc_owns_userpd(ab))
+		return ath12k_ahb_boot_root_pd(ab);
+
 	rmem = ath12k_core_get_reserved_mem(ab, 0);
 	if (!rmem)
 		return -ENODEV;
@@ -470,6 +502,11 @@
 	u32 pasid;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (ath12k_ahb_rproc_owns_userpd(ab)) {
+		rproc_shutdown(ab_ahb->tgt_rproc);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	qcom_smem_state_update_bits(ab_ahb->stop_state, BIT(ab_ahb->stop_bit),
 				    BIT(ab_ahb->stop_bit));
 
@@ -881,6 +918,14 @@
 		goto err_put_rproc;
 	}
 
+	/* Leave the boot to ath12k_ahb_power_up() so that the firmware only
+	 * starts once this driver is ready for it. Booting it here instead
+	 * lets the QMI handshake begin during probe, and the firmware then
+	 * takes a fatal error shortly after coming up.
+	 */
+	if (ath12k_ahb_rproc_owns_userpd(ab))
+		return 0;
+
 	if (ab_ahb->tgt_rproc->state != RPROC_RUNNING) {
 		ret = ath12k_ahb_boot_root_pd(ab);
 		if (ret < 0) {
